# Galaxy Survivor in preproduction (pre.elclub.party/galaxy). Copy to /opt/elclub/pre/galaxy.env on the homelab
# (chmod 600, owned by the runner user) and fill the empty values; never commit the filled file. Read at runtime only
# (compose env_file): nothing here is baked into the image. Procedure: games/galaxy/docs/DEPLOY_PRE.md.
#
# Postgres straight on the supabase_default network as the galaxy_api role (only sees schema galaxy). The migration
# creates the role without a password; set one once (DEPLOY_PRE.md step 1) and put it here. sslmode=disable: the
# connection never leaves the Docker network.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://galaxy_api:@db:5432/postgres?sslmode=disable
# Exact origins allowed on POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE (CSRF guard). Comma-separated, no trailing slash.
GALAXY_PUBLIC_ORIGINS=https://pre.elclub.party
# AES-256-GCM key for the admins' TOTP secrets at rest: `openssl rand -base64 32`. Rotating it invalidates every
# enrolled authenticator: re-enrol each admin with `node dist/cli.js reset-totp <usuario>` (DEPLOY_PRE.md).
GALAXY_TOTP_KEY=
NODE_ENV=production
# The resource shop's Stripe keys (shop and lab plan, F4). Optional: empty, or not all three of one mode, the shop
# stays closed (the log says stripe_off or stripe_env_incomplete) and nothing else changes. A restricted key
# (rk_live_…), the webhook's signing secret (whsec_…) and the publishable key (pk_live_…). Steps: DEPLOY_PRE.md.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
